WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:18.370
Introduced by Christian Heinrich von Nagel in eighteen thirty-six, X nine is the Mittenpunkt— literally the middle point: the concurrence of the three lines joining the excenters J sub a, J sub b, and J sub c to the corresponding side midpoints M sub a, M sub b, and M sub c.

2
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:23.359
Geometrically, X nine is the symmedian point of the excentral triangle.

3
00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:36.421
Its trilinear distances are proportional to the semiperimeter excesses, s minus a, to s minus b, to s minus c, and its barycentric areas are a times s minus a, to b times s minus b, to c times s minus c.

4
00:00:36.421 --> 00:00:45.880
On the central lines layer, X nine lies at the intersection of line X one X six, line X two X seven, and the Orthocenter–Spieker line X four X ten.

5
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:56.020
Under functional relations, X nine is the complement of the Gergonne point X seven, the isogonal conjugate of X fifty-seven, and the isotomic conjugate of X eighty-five.
